md += ['','Ten retiered checkpoint questions now explicitly record their existing checkpointPool. This uses the established stage-versus-difficulty mechanism; it does not move any checkpoint. Eight ordinary questions move between existing cognitive-tier pools. The old sourcePool, originalSourcePool, instructionalRole, prerequisites, and modeAllowlist remain exact on all 42 records.','','## Rewrites, strengthening and family progression','','- LG-Q-9123 now derives inflation across two periods, applies a backward-looking nominal-wage rule, and diagnoses purchasing-power losses and the compensating raise. PM2C2-NEUT-FB-004 retains its distinct level-versus-growth task without the arbitrary resource index.','- LG-Q-9107 now reconciles a reserve drain, a partially offsetting reserve-ratio cut, and the lending incentive from higher interest on reserves under stated hypothetical assumptions.','- LG-Q-9122 now reconciles independent measurements across two periods and computes inflation from corrected values.','- PM2B4-UTYPE-LB-001 calculates search stocks from flows and duration, then distinguishes matching assistance from retraining and demand stimulus. The canonical Hard classification/remedy item stays unchanged; its other named copies now diagnose technology/skills adjustment, cyclical versus natural unemployment, or evidence for retraining.','- Monetary transmission progresses from one failed rate-to-investment link, through reserve retention plus crowding out, to reconciling a reserve-removal target and cumulative disinflation costs. Existing checkpoint prerequisites are preserved.','- The diminishing-returns family now distinguishes human-capital improvement, marginal versus average output, comparative catch-up gains and invalid extrapolation, and multi-economy productivity convergence. ECON-NL-MEDIUMBOSS-3026 is retained as the one basic physical-capital diagnosis.','- LG-Q-9139 remains unchanged. LG-Q-9069 instead solves backward for policy size and re-evaluates it when monetary policy changes the crowding-out offset.','- CPI tasks distinguish a substitution-bias gap, the amount and interpretation of indexed-payment overcompensation, and combined quality/new-goods measurement. The accepted new-goods item remains unchanged.','- Real-interest tasks progress from one Fisher calculation, to expected/realized comparison, ranking, and borrower/lender surprise interpretation. The Legendary task integrates ranking reversal with opposite redistribution across the two economies. The existing Hard ranking item remains unchanged.','','## Route, tag and feedback corrections','','PMOE-RER-L-003 stays in the existing real-exchange-rate concept, uses the existing infer_nominal_change_from_real_stability skill/objective, and has an unambiguous real-exchange-rate display tag. It now supplies the approximation and quotation direction. The obsolete unused skill was removed from that concept’s faculty-outcome partition; no new taxonomy was invented. ECON-SP-MEDIUMBOSS-3011 uses the existing monetary_policy_transmission skill, repair skill and LO35.2 objective, with a monetary-policy tag; its checkpoint placement and prerequisites remain unchanged. P76-MODL-EL-003 was verified against its existing models-and-assumptions / model_selection route and needs no routing change.','','PM2A-LRPC-L-011 feedback now explains full anticipation, elimination of the inflation surprise, and the muted or absent temporary unemployment response. Every rewritten record received feedback tied to its final mechanism and numbers.','','## Shared areas, Market Gate and Micro freeze','','The exact directed P77-MVM-L-020 and P76-MODL-EL-003 retierings apply consistently to their existing General + Macro membership. Their stems, choices, keys, feedback and skills are unchanged. All other General canonical and published records remain exact. P77-MVM-L-021 was inspected and retained: the faculty specified inspection of the pair, not another General retiering or family rewrite. No affected record belongs to Micro. All 6,297 accepted Micro records and their full student publication projection remain exact; all 541 protected Macro Market Gate records remain exact. Negative controls reject unauthorized protected edits and routing mutations.','','## Graph freeze','','All 107 active Macro graph/image hashes match the accepted verification baseline. The complete canonical asset inventory and all 235 inventory hashes also match. No graph bytes, labels, colors or graph metadata changed. PG5-PC-L-024 retains its graph, supplied expectations rule, correctly derived slope, sequential inflation values and later unemployment constraint. No graph-accessibility audit was repeated.','','## Independent economics and numerical validation','',f"{num['checks']} independent arithmetic checks across {num['questionCount']} changed or explicitly retained numerical tasks passed. They cover monetary balances, quantity identities, wage growth, exchange quotations, expected/actual real returns and inflation surprises, marginal/average production, job-search stocks, sacrifice ratios, CPI quality adjustment/indexation, fiscal policy sizing, and the retained Phillips/fiscal examples. Qualitative checks distinguish nominal from real, flows from stocks, structural from frictional/cyclical unemployment, level from growth, and gross from net policy transmission. Assumptions and approximations are stated where needed.",'','The reserve-rate explanation was checked against the Federal Reserve’s description of reserve remuneration as an opportunity-cost/short-rate channel. The hypothetical reserve-ratio calculation is explicitly scoped and is not presented as a current institutional requirement. [Federal Reserve, ample-reserves implementation](https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/notes/feds-notes/implementing-monetary-policy-in-an-ample-reserves-regime-the-basics-note-1-of-3-20200701.html).','','## Answer, publication and test integrity','','Changed answer text uses the official core.normalizeAnswerText pipeline and SHA-256 mapping. All final keys resolve uniquely, with four distinct same-domain options. The exact revision chain reconstructs the entire accepted pre-closure library before replaying the earlier accepted contracts; there are no broad question-ID exemptions.','',f"All {len(passed)} current validation suites (the prior 29 plus the new exact closure suite) and all 25 exporter tests pass. The new suite includes the explicit faculty tiers, approved open-economy stem/key, exact retained records, retier-only content freezes, stage preservation, route corrections, linked-operation checks and negative controls.",'','The first run exposed missing explicit checkpoint-stage metadata and an unused old exchange-rate skill in the outcome partition. Both were corrected through existing metadata mechanisms, with no runtime refactor. All final tests were then rerun. General, Micro and Macro student builds compile and validate all ten current modes, answer resolution and publication parity. Existing canonical-to-all-course publication omissions remain unchanged and are enumerated in publication-validation.json. All three faculty PDF/CSV pairs regenerated. Every exported CSV stem, choice, feedback and answer matches canonical content; all 42 changed Macro PDF stem/key blocks pass extraction checks. Ten representative pages, including the retained graph, were rendered and visually inspected. No changed stem duplicates another current stem exactly or after numeric normalization; the check was limited to the 25 changed stems as comparison targets.','','## Remaining decisions and stop condition','','Remaining faculty decisions: **0**. The old candidate CSV remains historical evidence of the original proposals; the new closure CSV supersedes its pending status. No changes were made outside the 30 decisions, explicitly named diversification siblings, and their direct metadata/test dependencies. No new broad review was initiated. No commit, push or deployment was performed.','','## Deliverables and evidence','','- macro_faculty_candidate_closure_20261006.csv: 30 completed dispositions.','- macroeconomics_faculty_closure_changes_20261006.csv and .json: all 42 exact changes and authority.','- This report; regenerated faculty PDFs/CSVs.','- audit_tools/macro_faculty_closure_20261006/: compact canonical baseline, patch source, exact expectations, scope, numerical/publication/export proofs and logs. Local generated artifacts are ignored by Git; rollback evidence is retained.','',f"Final library SHA-256: `{N['librarySha256']}`."]
